    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup for 2026-08-01 leans heavily on advantageous matchups against mid-rotation arms to bolster our efficiency. Our strongest play is undoubtedly **Jacob Wilson** (74.08), whose leadoff spot and favorable matchup against the lefty Valdez create a high-ceiling environment. Similarly, **Cole Carrigg** (71.23) and **Drake Baldwin** (70.88) are essential starts; **Carrigg** benefits from an elite park factor and a weak opposing pitcher, while **Baldwin** leverages his leadoff duties and favorable xwOBA metrics to command the C1 slot. These three represent our primary engine for runs and batting average today. **Jackson Merrill** (69.10) also remains a core asset, as his platoon advantage against the right-handed Mahle allows him to maintain a high efficiency rating despite a slightly negative park adjustment.\n\nWe are navigating a few situational hurdles, most notably with **Gunnar Henderson** (53.01) and **Coby Mayo** (56.20). While both are talented, they face a formidable opponent in S\u00e1nchez. Their scores are artificially suppressed by the pitcher\u2019s skill and a tough catcher pop-time/hold-rate combination, though the wind blowing out at the venue provides a necessary lift to their power profiles. Meanwhile, **Denzer Guzman** (44.21) remains our most difficult bench decision; he provided a respectable floor but was ultimately relegated to the bench because his projected output was eclipsed by the more favorable order positions and platoon dynamics of starters like **Nasim Nunez** (62.50) and **Dominic Smith** (59.48). \n\nRisk management remains a priority given our 5x5 constraints, particularly regarding stolen base threats. While we have prioritized players like **Nasim Nunez** and **Cole Carrigg** to address our scarcity in speed, we must monitor **Andy Pages** (53.37) and **Gunnar Henderson**, as opposing catchers with elite pop times and pitchers with high hold percentages continue to depress the expected value of our base-stealing attempts. **Jordan Westburg** remains unavailable on the IL, requiring us to extract maximum value from our remaining healthy depth to maintain our competitive edge in the standings.",
